a statute kind row (amalek_remembrance_declared) fields: ['remember_what_amalek_did_to_you', 'how_he_met_you', 'when_the_lord_gives_you_rest', 'blot_out_the_memory_of_amalek', 'you_shall_not_forget'] | form statute | corpus deu_22_return_sex_laws (STEP_Dt_22_1 through STEP_Dt_22_29; claims DV22-01 through DV22-05), deu_23_qahal_purity_vows (STEP_Dt_23_1 through STEP_Dt_23_26; claims DV23-01 through DV23-05), deu_24_divorce_poor (STEP_Dt_24_1 through STEP_Dt_24_22; claims DV24-01 through DV24-05) and deu_25_courts_yibbum (STEP_Dt_25_1 through STEP_Dt_25_19; claims DV25-01 through DV25-05) | whole row: {'en': "Amalek's remembrance declared — 'REMEMBER WHAT AMALEK DID TO YOU in the way when you came out of Egypt: how he met you in the way and cut off your rear, all the stragglers behind you, when you were faint and weary, and he feared not God. And it shall be, WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU REST from all your enemies around, in the land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance to possess it, YOU SHALL BLOT OUT THE MEMORY OF AMALEK FROM UNDER HEAVEN; YOU SHALL NOT FORGET' (Deut 25:17-19) — remember with the mouth, do not forget in the heart (296:1, 296:9); the three remembrances' one phrase; met you by chance, by cooling, by nocturnal uncleanness — the three homographs (296:2-3); the stragglers (Onkelos); he feared not God — the one God of the four chapters; the tape's amalek_came at Exodus 17:8 the readback's reference (a retelling, never a second act); the three commandments on entering — the king, Amalek, the house (296:5-6); the rest 1 Samuel 15's clock the run's citation AHEAD, a pointer owed; the gift formula's seat; amalek_to_be_blotted Exodus 17:14's heaven entry on Amalek the tape's reference — the command on Israel written HERE; THE TWO BLOTTINGS — Amalek's memory and the dead brother's name (296:9; 25:6's twin); you shall not forget twice in the Torah (25:19, 31:21); forgetting_barred 8:11's the reference, a new block on Amalek's memory: the line writes amalek_remembrance_commanded and amalek_memory_blotting_commanded (STATUSES) and amalek_forgetting_barred (a BLOCK) on israel_people", 'he': 'זָכוֹר אֵת אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה לְךָ עֲמָלֵק בַּדֶּרֶךְ בְּצֵאתְכֶם מִמִּצְרָֽיִם (remember what Amalek did to you in the way when you came out of Egypt — Deut 25:17) · אֲשֶׁר קָֽרְךָ בַּדֶּרֶךְ וַיְזַנֵּב בְּךָ כָּל הַנֶּחֱשָׁלִים אַֽחַרֶיךָ וְאַתָּה עָיֵף וְיָגֵעַ וְלֹא יָרֵא אֱלֹהִֽים (the verse continues — Deut 25:18) · וְהָיָה בְּהָנִיחַ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְךָ מִכָּל אֹיְבֶיךָ מִסָּבִיב בָּאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר יְהוָֽה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לְךָ נַחֲלָה לְרִשְׁתָּהּ תִּמְחֶה אֶת זֵכֶר עֲמָלֵק מִתַּחַת הַשָּׁמָיִם לֹא תִּשְׁכָּֽח (the verse continues — Deut 25:19)', 'form': 'statute', 'witness': ['Deut 25:17 | זכור את אשר עשה לך עמלק בדרך בצאתכם ממצרים', 'Deut 25:18 | אשר קרך בדרך ויזנב בך כל הנחשלים אחריך ואתה עיף ויגע ולא ירא אלהים', 'Deut 25:19 | והיה בהניח יהוה אלהיך לך מכל איביך מסביב בארץ אשר יהוה אלהיך נתן לך נחלה לרשתה תמחה את זכר עמלק מתחת השמים לא תשכח', 'Exod 17:8 | ויבא עמלק וילחם עם ישראל ברפידם', 'Exod 17:14 | ויאמר יהוה אל משה כתב זאת זכרון בספר ושים באזני יהושע כי מחה אמחה את זכר עמלק מתחת השמים', 'Exod 17:15 | ויבן משה מזבח ויקרא שמו יהוה נסי', 'Exod 17:16 | ויאמר כי יד על כס יה מלחמה ליהוה בעמלק מדר דר', 'Deut 8:11 | השמר לך פן תשכח את יהוה אלהיך לבלתי שמר מצותיו ומשפטיו וחקתיו אשר אנכי מצוך היום'], 'ink': "Deut 22:1-25:19; Onkelos Deut 22:1-29, 23:1-26, 24:1-22 and 25:1-19 (the export's four chapters the DB's — the identity in both; 96 rows); the Sifrei on Deuteronomy ON THE FOUR CHAPTERS — piskaot 222-296 (the spine whole, 434 rows in both files; five headless: 222 on 22:1 (opening on Exodus 23:5), 236 on 22:16-17 (inside the father's words), 269 on 24:1 (the grounds of divorce), 283 on 24:19 (the forgotten sheaf), 295 on 25:16) with the rows elsewhere citing the chapters (piskaot 41, 63, 87, 94, 110, 117, 122, 155, 190, 336, 352 — ten reread, four excluded); THE LEAN PASS (owner-ruled 2026-09-23): no docket — the exam the forty-four Mishnah rows the ledger cites at least twice (Bava Batra 5:10, 5:11; Bava Kamma 8:1, 8:3; Bava Metzia 2:7, 2:8, 2:9, 2:10, 5:10, 9:13; Berakhot 3:5; Chullin 12:2, 12:3; Gittin 2:4, 3:1, 8:1, 9:10; Ketubot 3:1, 3:5, 4:3; Kiddushin 1:1; Makkot 3:10, 3:15; Peah 4:6, 6:6, 7:2; Rosh Hashanah 1:1; Sanhedrin 3:4, 11:1; Sotah 7:2, 8:4; Temurah 6:2, 6:3; Yevamot 1:1, 2:1, 3:9, 4:13, 8:2, 8:3, 10:1, 12:1, 12:3, 12:6; Zavim 2:3), logic/oral_triage/deu_22_25_ki_teitzei_exam_2026-09-26.md; the full process owed", 'corpus': 'deu_22_return_sex_laws (STEP_Dt_22_1 through STEP_Dt_22_29; claims DV22-01 through DV22-05), deu_23_qahal_purity_vows (STEP_Dt_23_1 through STEP_Dt_23_26; claims DV23-01 through DV23-05), deu_24_divorce_poor (STEP_Dt_24_1 through STEP_Dt_24_22; claims DV24-01 through DV24-05) and deu_25_courts_yibbum (STEP_Dt_25_1 through STEP_Dt_25_19; claims DV25-01 through DV25-05)', 'tape': "submitted by cold_run_persons_poor_court.py [subjects: moses (to israel)] (the narrative scene, THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 17b — LEAN); re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consumed by law_persons_poor_court (cold_run_persons_poor_court.py) -> amalek_remembrance_commanded, amalek_memory_blotting_commanded on israel_people (STATUSES — the three on entering a data row; amalek_to_be_blotted one on amaleq and amalek_weakened the tape's references; the run 1 Samuel 15's, a pointer owed), amalek_forgetting_barred (a BLOCK — forgetting_barred 8:11's the reference); at the counter's day (40, 11, 1), no marker", 'fields': ['remember_what_amalek_did_to_you', 'how_he_met_you', 'when_the_lord_gives_you_rest', 'blot_out_the_memory_of_amalek', 'you_shall_not_forget']}
an effect row whole (amalek_forgetting_barred): {'en': "forgetting Amalek barred — the BLOCK the line amalek_remembrance_declared writes on Israel: 'YOU SHALL NOT FORGET' (25:19) — do not forget in the heart, remember with the mouth (the Sifrei 296:9 — the two organs the data row); you shall not forget twice in the Torah (25:19, 31:21 — the reading's find 10); forgetting_barred one on israel_people (8:11's line) the tape's reference — the formula's second seat a new block on Amalek's memory, not a second write", 'he': 'לֹא תִּשְׁכָּֽח (you shall not forget — Deut 25:19)', 'ledger_op': 'block', 'ink': "Deut 25:19, 8:11 (good_land — the formula's first seat, the reference), 31:21; Onkelos 25:19; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 296:9", 'corpus': 'deu_22_return_sex_laws (STEP_Dt_22_1 through STEP_Dt_22_29; claims DV22-01 through DV22-05), deu_23_qahal_purity_vows (STEP_Dt_23_1 through STEP_Dt_23_26; claims DV23-01 through DV23-05), deu_24_divorce_poor (STEP_Dt_24_1 through STEP_Dt_24_22; claims DV24-01 through DV24-05) and deu_25_courts_yibbum (STEP_Dt_25_1 through STEP_Dt_25_19; claims DV25-01 through DV25-05)', 'exam': 'cold_run_persons_poor_court.py (F16 amalek — you_shall_not_forget; the line amalek_remembrance_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the forty-four Mishnah rows the ledger cites at least twice (deu_22_25_ki_teitzei_exam_2026-09-26.md)'} | (righteousness_before_the_lord): {'en': "righteousness before the LORD — the HEAVEN entry the line pledge_wage_declared writes on Israel: 'AND IT SHALL BE RIGHTEOUSNESS TO YOU BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD' (24:13) — righteousness before the throne, Psalm 85:14 cited (the Sifrei 277:5 — the reading's find 9); Onkelos merit (zekhuta) for righteousness (the reading's find 15); the returned pledge's heaven", 'he': 'וּלְךָ תִּהְיֶה צְדָקָה לִפְנֵי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ (and it shall be righteousness to you before the LORD your God — Deut 24:13)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': "Deut 24:13, 6:25 (hear_o_israel — the word's other seat), Genesis 15:6 (the count of righteousness); Onkelos 24:13; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 277:5", 'corpus': 'deu_22_return_sex_laws (STEP_Dt_22_1 through STEP_Dt_22_29; claims DV22-01 through DV22-05), deu_23_qahal_purity_vows (STEP_Dt_23_1 through STEP_Dt_23_26; claims DV23-01 through DV23-05), deu_24_divorce_poor (STEP_Dt_24_1 through STEP_Dt_24_22; claims DV24-01 through DV24-05) and deu_25_courts_yibbum (STEP_Dt_25_1 through STEP_Dt_25_19; claims DV25-01 through DV25-05)', 'exam': 'cold_run_persons_poor_court.py (F11 the_pledge_and_the_wage — righteousness_before_the_lord; the line pledge_wage_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the forty-four Mishnah rows the ledger cites at least twice (deu_22_25_ki_teitzei_exam_2026-09-26.md)'} | (blessings_for_hearing): {'en': "the blessings for hearing — the conditional HEAVEN entry the chapter's second line writes on Israel (the form of treasured_people — Exodus 19:5-6's 'if you will hear My voice and keep My covenant' read back at 7:12): 'because you hear these judgments and keep and do them, the LORD your God will keep for you the covenant and the kindness which he swore to your fathers' (7:12 — 'because' the heel as a conjunction, the five seats; Onkelos 'in exchange for'), the blessing's list (7:13 — the fruit of the womb and of the ground, the grain, the wine and the oil, the increase of the cattle and the young of the flock: 28:4, 11, 18, 51 forward; the flock's word tagged a name in the DB's morphology), 'blessed above all peoples' (7:14 — no barren, Exodus 23:26's clause restated; Bekhorot 44b), the sickness removed (7:15 — Exodus 15:26's healer TURNED: the diseases of Egypt laid on those who hate you; 28:60 forward; Bava Metzia 107b the evil eye); the entry OPEN on the condition; written on the counter's day (40, 11, 1), no marker", 'he': 'וְשָׁמַר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְךָ אֶֽת הַבְּרִית וְאֶת הַחֶסֶד (the LORD your God will keep for you the covenant and the kindness — Deut 7:12)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': "Deut 7:12-15; Exodus 19:5-6 (the offer's condition — the tape's covenant_offered), 23:25-26 (the bread and water blessed, no barren — ordinances.land by CALL), 15:26 (the healer's condition — exodus_story.marah by CALL); Deut 28:4, 11, 18, 51, 60 (forward); Onkelos 7:12-15; Babylonian Talmud Bekhorot 44b:7, Bava Metzia 107b:2, Berakhot 51b:5, Chullin 84b:1; THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 13b (2026-09-23): Deut 15:5 THE REUSE — the chapter's line release_law_declared writes A SECOND ENTRY on israel_people at the counter's day (40, 11, 1): the release's blessing conditional on the hearing — אִם שָׁמוֹעַ תִּשְׁמַע בְּקוֹל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ (if only you diligently hearken to the voice of the LORD your God — Deut 15:5); 28:1's header fourteen of seventeen in order, 11:13's second paragraph the same form (the Sifrei 114:1-115:2 — the blessing only in the Land, the conquest first; 'hear, you shall hear' the words of the scribes); 8b's lesson: a reused effect is a second entry on the same ledger (CQ6's, DC6's, Q21's and Q30's ONE retyped TWO)", 'corpus': 'deu_07_nations_cherem (STEP_Dt_7_12 through STEP_Dt_7_15; the claims DV07-01 through DV07-06)', 'exam': "cold_run_seven_nations.py (F4 because_you_hear — covenant_kept, the_blessing_list, no_barren, the_diseases; the exam kind seven_nations_case; the entry written on the tape kind hearing_blessed); THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 13b (2026-09-23): cold_run_release_firstborn.py (F2 the_needy_and_the_blessing — the_hearkening; the reuse's second entry written on the tape kind release_law_declared)"}
